    "updated_at": "2022-06-05T00:07:16Z",
    "body": "This can only happen if installing as root, but the fix of setting the owner to root looks easy.\r\n\r\nHowever, while investigating this I think I also found two bugs in the install script's `test_writeable` function. First, it will update the date/time on an existing `$BIN_DIR/test.txt`; second, and related, if that file exists then we're only testing that that file is writeable, not that the directory is writeable. The solution is to find a filename that _doesn't_ exist (`test.txt` is a good choice, but then if it does exist try `test.txt.1`, `test.txt.2`, ...) and then try to create it.",
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
    "pin": null,
